# Both worlds
> vsh runs the Unix commands in UP-Term:bin first, then the AmigaDOS commands of the
> Shell's path, so Dir, Assign and Version still work from vsh. Two names are special:
> vsh's `type` and `which` builtins shadow the AmigaDOS C:Type command, which you reach as `C:Type`.
> From the AmigaDOS Shell you start vsh by typing `vsh` in an XCON: window.
? Ask where the command ls comes from, with which.
= case "$LEARN_LINE" in "which ls") true ;; *) false ;; esac
~ Type which ls.
! which ls
? Run the AmigaDOS command Version.
= case "$LEARN_LINE" in [Vv]ersion) true ;; *) false ;; esac
~ Type Version (upper or lower case).
! Version
